  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions using Dijkstra\u2019s algorithm for each distinct source, with results reused for repeated sources.\n\n- [Rust](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/routes/rust/src/main.rs) uses a compact contiguous adjacency structure and a binary heap.\n- [plain.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/routes/plain.py) uses native Python adjacency lists and `heapq`.\n- [fast.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/routes/fast.py) uses NumPy to parse the input, then native integers for graph traversal.\n\nAll three versions pass **s1, s2 and s3**, as well as 20 randomized graphs checked against an independent shortest-path calculation. The Rust release build completed offline.",
